# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE -- the UNIT_LENGTH BOHR
# counterpart of lih_gnof_full_optimization.inp, same system, same functional, same geometry
# (1.594900 Angstrom = 3.01392419749269 Bohr), given here directly in Bohr instead of the
# default Angstrom. UNIT_LENGTH BOHR (or AU, an accepted synonym) is applied after the whole
# input file is parsed, so it works regardless of where it appears relative to GEOMETRY.
# Converged energies match lih_gnof_full_optimization.inp's exactly (same physical geometry,
# just given in different units) -- a routine cross-check that the unit conversion is correct.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
UNIT_LENGTH BOHR
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
USE_RI FALSE  # preserve this example's pre-existing dense/Cholesky path (USE_RI now defaults TRUE)

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   3.01392419749269
END
